---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About">
  <section class="min-h-screen pt-32 pb-24 px-6 md:px-12 max-w-7xl mx-auto flex flex-col md:flex-row items-start gap-12 md:gap-24">
      
      <!-- Text (Left) -->
      <div class="flex-1 order-2 md:order-1">
          <h1 class="font-serif text-5xl md:text-6xl mb-4 italic">About Todd Margolis</h1>
          <p class="font-mono text-sm text-gray-400 mb-8 font-semibold">A Convergence of Art, Engineering, and Strategy</p>
          <div class="font-mono text-sm text-gray-300 space-y-6 leading-relaxed text-justify">
              <p>
                  Todd Margolis is a product strategist, researcher, and artist who has spent over two decades navigating the "uncomfortable in-betweens" of emerging technology. His career is defined by a unique ability to translate "blue sky" academic inquiry into scalable, market-ready realities. By synthesizing the rigor of computer science with the speculative capacity of new media art, he helps organizations and audiences grasp the layered infrastructures that shape our world.
              </p>

              <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-white mt-10 mb-4">The Engineering of Experience</h3>
              <p>
                  Todd's trajectory began at the bleeding edge of visualization research. As a grad student and then Visiting Research Programmer at the University of Illinois at Chicago's <strong class="text-white">Electronic Visualization Lab (EVL)</strong>, he co-invented the <strong class="text-white">Varrier™ auto-stereoscopic display</strong>—a pioneering barrier-strip system that enabled high-resolution Virtual Reality without the need for glasses. This early work in modeling sub-pixel rendering algorithms established the foundation of his practice: removing the friction between the user and the data.
              </p>
              <p>
                  He expanded this expertise as the <strong class="text-white">Technical Director</strong> of the <strong class="text-white">Center for Research in Computing and the Arts (CRCA)</strong> at UCSD. There, he spearheaded the design and architecture of a <strong class="text-white">10,000 sq. ft. research facility</strong>, managing labs dedicated to spatialized audio, motion capture, and immersive environments. He served as a bridge between diverse disciplines, leading interdisciplinary teams to build "discovery platforms" for massive datasets ranging from metagenomics to cultural analytics.
              </p>

              <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-white mt-10 mb-4">From Telepresence to Product Strategy</h3>
              <p>
                  What distinguishes Todd's approach to product management is his background in high-stakes, real-time media systems. Projects like <strong class="text-white">CineGrid 3D 4K</strong>—which successfully executed the tri-continental premiere of 4K feature-length media via optical networks <strong class="text-white">(in 2010)</strong> and his work in <strong class="text-white">Telepresence Performance</strong> (<em>TeleMotions</em>, <em>ResoNations</em>) required more than just creative vision; they demanded rigorous logistical planning, latency management, and fault-tolerant network architecture.
              </p>
              <p>
                  This experience in <strong class="text-white">Distributed Cinema</strong> and networked collaboration directly informs his data-driven approach to product leadership. He views enterprise software not merely as code, but as a collaborative environment where human intuition and algorithmic logic must coexist.
              </p>

              <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-white mt-10 mb-4">Applied Research & Innovation Leadership</h3>
              <p>
                  Today, as <strong class="text-white">Sr. Director of Applied Research & Emerging Technologies at Qlik</strong>, Todd accelerates the long-term roadmap for enterprise intelligence. He leads a team of machine learning engineers to define the strategy for <strong class="text-white">Generative AI</strong>, moving beyond the hype cycle to develop capabilities that are ethical, scalable, and genuinely useful.
              </p>
              <p>
                  His current artistic focus, <a href="http://observables.art">Observables</a>, continues this inquiry. Through projects like <em>Horizons</em> (a stereoscopic intervention into space data) and <em>Now & Then</em> (temporary astrophotography compositions), he continues to materialize the invisible, proving that the tools of rigorous research and the instruments of artistic expression are one and the same.
              </p>
          </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Portrait (Right) -->
      <div class="flex-1 order-1 md:order-2 w-full md:sticky md:top-32">
          <div class="aspect-[3/4] bg-gray-800 relative overflow-hidden">
              <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-indigo-900/20 mix-blend-overlay z-10"></div>
              <img src="/images/todd.jpeg" alt="Todd Margolis" class="w-full h-full object-cover grayscale hover:grayscale-0 transition-all duration-1000">
          </div>
      </div>

  </section>
</Layout>
